Tool.
  tool """" KeYmaera X """"
  model """" ArchiveEntry "pH Lyapunov M(1)<0 FULLY PARAMETRIC (general D1,K,d)"

/*
 * FULLY PARAMETERIZED positive result (no fixed numbers).
 *
 * Two-machine pH system, D1>0, K>0, D2=-d (d>0). pH Lyapunov function
 *   V = H + h*sin^2(delta) + a1*w1*sin(delta) + a2*w2*sin(delta)
 * with the PARAMETRIC coefficients
 *   a1 = D1+d,  a2 = (D1+3d)/2,  h = (6*D1^2+11*D1*d+15*d^2)/32.
 *
 * M(1) is the quadratic form of V'_lin at the equilibrium (c=1):
 *   M00=-2*D1+a1, M01=(a2-a1)/2, M02=(-a1*D1+2*h)/2
 *   M11=2*d-a2,   M12=(a2*d-2*h)/2, M22=K*(a2-a1)
 *
 * M(1)<0 iff -M(1)>0 iff the 3 leading principal minors of -M are positive.
 * Symbolic computation (general D1,K,d) gives them in CLOSED FORM:
 *   LM1 = D1 - d
 *   LM2 = 7*(D1-d)^2/16
 *   LM3 = 7*(D1-d)^3*(16*K-(2*D1+3*d)^2)/512
 *
 * THEOREM: for ALL D1,K,d with D1>0, K>0, 0<d<D1, (2*D1+3*d)^2<16*K,
 * the three minors are positive (so M(1)<0). This is the parametric
 * derivation of the sufficient condition (2*D1+3*d)^2<16*K, not a numeric
 * instance. (det_factorization.kyx proves the LM3 determinant identity;
 * here the full M(1)<0 condition is assembled and decided by QE.)
 */

ProgramVariables
  Real D1;
  Real K;
  Real d;
End.

Problem
  \forall D1 \forall K \forall d (
    ( D1 > 0 & K > 0 & d > 0 & d < D1 & (2*D1+3*d)^2 < 16*K )
    ->
    ( D1 - d > 0
    & 7*(D1-d)^2/16 > 0
    & 7*(D1-d)^3*(16*K-(2*D1+3*d)^2)/512 > 0 ) )
End.

Tactic "Proof"
  QE
End.

